---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals build custom finance or financial administration software?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Custom software can be developed around organisation-specific financial administration, approvals, transaction records, reporting and related operational workflows.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can financial workflows use role-based approvals?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Permissions, approval levels and workflow states can be designed around defined organisational responsibilities.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can finance software integrate with accounting, ERP or payment systems?",
    answer:
      "Where suitable APIs or supported integration mechanisms are available, financial and operational platforms can be connected. The exact integration should be assessed against the systems involved.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can repetitive finance administration be automated?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Defined tasks such as approval routing, notifications, document generation and selected data movement can often be automated where the underlying rules are stable.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can dashboards provide financial and operational reporting?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Reporting can be developed around reliable source data such as revenue, expenditure, receivables, project finance and other available business information.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does LKProfessionals guarantee financial-regulatory compliance?",
    answer:
      "No blanket compliance claim should be made. Regulatory and security requirements depend on the organisation, jurisdiction, data, infrastructure, third-party services and exact implementation. Those requirements must be assessed specifically for each project.",
  },
];
---

<section class="finance-faq">
  <div class="site-container finance-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Finance FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions to settle before automating a financial workflow.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="finance-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .finance-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .finance-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(17rem, 0.7fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .finance-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .finance-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .finance-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .finance-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .finance-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .finance-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .finance-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
